  "decision_conditions": [
    "The hip-to-gable roof alteration, by reason of its bulk and exacerbated by failure to use matching roof materials, viewed cumulatively with the front dormer and gable, gives rise to a visually heavy roof to one half of this semi-detached pair, which is out of character with the original property and its neighbouring pair, gives rise to a negative effect on the street scene by creating a loss of symmetry and is out of keeping with the predominant character of hipped roof slopes to semi-detached bungalows along Masefield Drive, which is contrary to the purposes and intent of Local Plan Policies 7, 26 and the Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document.",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy, notification of intended refusal and the reason(s) for it was given to the applicants via email on 18/02/2025."
